// The repository's Markdown lint configuration, seeded once by
// spec-driven-docs. The project owns this file: edit it freely, and a later
// landing keeps its bytes.
//
// It loads the relative-links rule, which fails a relative link whose target
// does not exist. Every other rule takes the linter's default here, and the
// documentation root's own configuration merges over this one beneath it.
//
// Put a Markdown path the linter must skip in `ignores`. The `reserved:` list
// in .spec-driven-docs/config.yaml scopes sdd's own gates, not this linter.
//
// vitals' choices:
// - MD013 is off, because dprint owns the line layout (textWrap: never).
// - GLOSSARY.md is rendered by release-kit, and a generated file follows its
//   generator. CLAUDE.md is the one-line import of AGENTS.md.
// - The UI snapshot files are written by pytest-textual-snapshot.
// - release-kit and spec-driven-docs land the agent skill packages
//   rk-release, rk-setup, sdd-setup, and sdd-write-docs under .claude/skills
//   and .agents/skills, and a byte changed there is drift. The project's own
//   skills in those roots stay under the checks.
{
  "customRules": ["markdownlint-rule-relative-links"],
  "config": {
    "relative-links": true,
    "MD013": false
  },
  "ignores": [
    "GLOSSARY.md",
    "CLAUDE.md",
    "tests/**/__snapshots__/**",
    ".claude/skills/rk-release/**",
    ".claude/skills/rk-setup/**",
    ".claude/skills/sdd-setup/**",
    ".claude/skills/sdd-write-docs/**",
    ".agents/skills/rk-release/**",
    ".agents/skills/rk-setup/**",
    ".agents/skills/sdd-setup/**",
    ".agents/skills/sdd-write-docs/**"
  ]
}
